From 1e9af42ed23b83b07ae60ea1397151fe618a1dec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:00:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(tools): lathe tool assemblies - nose-centre tip,
 orientation and clearance

A turning holder or boring bar with its insert (and adapters) resolves
to the nose centre as the tip of the turning frame, the derived
LinuxCNC orientation (1-8), the nose radius and the seat and insert
values, and one LatheClearance over all non-insert bodies. The spindle
chain is shared through tool_assembly::placed. Refusals are named:
fit, orientation, no nose radius, a revolved body, a body past the
cutting lines near the nose, and the clearance errors on the whole
stack.

Refs #3643

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
